#Terraform Interview questions (2-4 years DevOps Engineer)

You have multiple engineers working on Terraform. How will you prevent state conflicts and ensure safe collaboration?
Your Terraform state file got corrupted. How would you recover the infrastructure?
You need to deploy the same infrastructure in dev, staging, and production with minimal duplication. How would you design it?
An existing AWS infrastructure is already running manually. How will you bring it under Terraform management?
Your terraform apply failed after creating some resources. What steps will you take next?
You need to update a production resource without downtime. How would you handle it in Terraform?
How would you manage secrets like DB passwords securely in Terraform?
You notice a drift between Terraform state and actual infrastructure. How will you detect and fix it?
How will you structure a Terraform project for a large microservices-based application?
You need to reuse infrastructure code across multiple teams/projects. How would you design it?
Explain how Terraform handles dependency resolution internally.
What is the lifecycle block? Explain real use cases of create_before_destroy and prevent_destroy.
How does Terraform ensure idempotency?
What is the difference between count and for_each in real production scenarios?
How does remote backend configuration work? Explain with locking mechanism.
What are provisioners? Why should they be avoided in production?
What is the purpose of terraform import and its limitations?
Explain Terraform workspaces and when you should NOT use them.
What is a data source in Terraform and how is it different from a resource?
How do you optimize Terraform performance for large infrastructures?
